    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <cstdio>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <climits>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n\\nclass FastScanner {\\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\\n    int idx, size;\\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\\npublic:\\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\\n    inline int nextInt() {\\n        char c;\\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ' && c);\\n        int sign = 1;\\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\\n        long long x = 0;\\n        for (; c >= '0' && c <= '9'; c = getChar()) {\\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\\n        }\\n        return static_cast<int>(sign * x);\\n    }\\nprivate:\\n    inline char getChar() {\\n        if (idx >= size) {\\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\\n            idx = 0;\\n            if (size == 0) return '\\\\0';\\n        }\\n        return buf[idx++];\\n    }\\n};\\n\\nint main() {\\n    FastScanner fs;\\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\\n\\n    std::vector<int> a(static_cast<size_t>(n) * n);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        int* row = &a[static_cast<size_t>(i) * n];\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n            row[j] = fs.nextInt();\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    long long mxSum = -(1LL << 62);\\n    const int totalRows = n - s + 1;\\n\\n#pragma omp parallel reduction(max:mxSum)\\n    {\\n        const int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\\n        const int nt = omp_get_num_threads();\\n\\n        std::vector<long long> v(n);\\n        std::vector<long long> pref(n + 1);\\n\\n        const int q = totalRows / nt;\\n        const int r = totalRows % nt;\\n        const int base = q * tid + (tid < r ? tid : r);\\n        const int len = q + (tid < r ? 1 : 0);\\n\\n        if (len > 0) {\\n            long long* __restrict vp = v.data();\\n#pragma omp simd\\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n                vp[j] = 0;\\n            }\\n            for (int k = 0; k < s; ++k) {\\n                const int* __restrict rowPtr = &a[static_cast<size_t>(base + k) * n];\\n#pragma omp simd\\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n                    vp[j] += static_cast<long long>(rowPtr[j]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            pref[0] = 0;\\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n                pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + v[i];\\n            }\\n            long long rowBest = LLONG_MIN;\\n#pragma omp simd reduction(max:rowBest)\\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\\n                const long long w = pref[j + s] - pref[j];\\n                if (w > rowBest) rowBest = w;\\n            }\\n            if (rowBest > mxSum) mxSum = rowBest;\\n\\n            for (int idx = 1; idx < len; ++idx) {\\n                const int outRow = base + idx - 1;\\n                const int inRow = outRow + s;\\n                const int* __restrict inPtr = &a[static_cast<size_t>(inRow) * n];\\n                const int* __restrict outPtr = &a[static_cast<size_t>(outRow) * n];\\n#pragma omp simd\\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n                    vp[j] += static_cast<long long>(inPtr[j]) - outPtr[j];\\n                }\\n\\n                pref[0] = 0;\\n                for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n                    pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + v[i];\\n                }\\n                long long rowBest2 = LLONG_MIN;\\n#pragma omp simd reduction(max:rowBest2)\\n                for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\\n                    const long long w = pref[j + s] - pref[j];\\n                    if (w > rowBest2) rowBest2 = w;\\n                }\\n                if (rowBest2 > mxSum) mxSum = rowBest2;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    std::printf(\\\"%lld\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Restructuring the initial column-sum computation from a column-major nested loop (outer over columns, inner over rows) into row-major accumulation with an explicit SIMD pragma on each row pass improves cache locality and enables vectorization across contiguous elements. This legal transformation preserves all dependencies while reducing memory-access overhead for the per-thread startup phase.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Only src/solution.cpp is modified. The change replaces the original nested loop (for j { for k ... }) with a zero-initialized SIMD loop followed by s separate row-wise SIMD accumulation loops, each reading contiguous ints and writing to long long v[]. All other logic remains identical: same sliding-window column updates, prefix sums, horizontal max reductions, and OpenMP parallelization. The transformation is purely a loop-order/vectorization improvement with no algorithmic change.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Restructured initial column-sum nested loop into row-major accumulation\",\n    \"Added explicit #pragma omp simd to zero-init and per-row accumulation loops\",\n    \"Introduced __restrict qualifiers for v and row pointers in the initialization phase\"\n  ]\n}",
    "thinking": "We need to propose one bounded HPC source-code experiment. Role B: legal SIMD/vectorization and loop dependencies. We have current source at src/solution.cpp. Need to modify only that file. Goal is performance improvement while preserving correctness.\n\nCurrent implementation: O(N^2) algorithm with column sums sliding window, parallelized over rows (totalRows = n-s+1). Each thread handles a contiguous chunk of starting row indices. For each start row base+idx, it computes initial column sum v[j] for first s rows, then slides down by adding inRow and subtracting outRow per column. Then prefix sums to compute horizontal window max.\n\nPotential improvements:\n- The inner sliding loop updates v[j] with omp simd; good.\n- Prefix scan is sequential dependency but short (n up to 8000). Could vectorize? Not easily due to recurrence.\n- Horizontal max reduction uses omp simd reduction(max:rowBest) - that's fine.\n\nMaybe we can improve by using a different algorithm: compute column sums for all rows first, then use sliding window horizontally. But current is already O(N^2).\n\nCould try to reduce overhead of prefix scan per row? Maybe combine horizontal max with the update loop without storing pref? Actually need prefix to get sum over s consecutive columns. Could maintain a running sum as we slide horizontally: For each row, compute initial window sum for j=0..s-1, then slide right by adding v[j+s] and subtracting v[j]. That avoids prefix array entirely! This is O(N) per row with simple operations, no dependency chain except the sliding recurrence which can be vectorized? Actually the horizontal sliding has a loop-carried dependency (window sum depends on previous), but we could unroll or use SIMD by computing all window sums in parallel using prefix? But prefix itself is sequential. However, current approach uses prefix to compute each window sum independently: w = pref[j+s] - pref[j], which allows vectorization across j because no loop-carried dependenc